g his upcoming concert in Indore. Authorities cited worries over the songs' promotion of liquor and violence, especially regarding children's impact. The District Child Protection Officer received a complaint highlighting these concerns and the guidelines from the Punjab and Haryana High Court. Additionally, restrictions include limitations on children on stage and the singer's costume.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/diljit-dosanjh-barred-from-singing-patiala-peg-3-other-songs-at-indore-concert-amid-child-safety-concerns/articleshow/135637930.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/diljit-dosanjh-barred-from-singing-patiala-peg-3-other-songs-at-indore-concert-amid-child-safety-concerns/articleshow/135637930.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-07T18:44:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135637968,imgsize-43772.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Ask Karnataka to seek consent of co-basin states': Tamil Nadu CM Vijay urges PM Modi over Mekedatu dam project]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ask-karnataka-to-seek-consent-of-co-basin-states-tamil-nadu-cm-vijay-urges-pm-modi-over-mekedatu-dam-project/articleshow/135637506.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135637506.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ask-karnataka-to-seek-consent-of-co-basin-states-tamil-nadu-cm-vijay-urges-pm-modi-over-mekedatu-dam-project/articleshow/135637506.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ask-karnataka-to-seek-consent-of-co-basin-states-tamil-nadu-cm-vijay-urges-pm-modi-over-mekedatu-dam-project/articleshow/135637506.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-07T18:43:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135637841,imgsize-220770.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ayodhya glows with 30 lakh diyas as Deepotsav lights up Saryu ghats on Diwali eve]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ayodhya-glows-with-30-lakh-diyas-as-deepotsav-lights-up-saryu-ghats-on-diwali-eve/articleshow/135637323.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135637323.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Lakhs of diyas illuminated Ram Ki Paidi ghat, while more than 30 lakh earthen lamps were set to light up 56 ghats along the river, turning the temple town into a spectacular sea of lights. The annual celebration, which marks return of Lord Ram to Ayodhya after defeating Ravana, recreates the traditional welcome believed to have been given to him by the people of the city in the Treta Yuga.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ayodhya-glows-with-30-lakh-diyas-as-deepotsav-lights-up-saryu-ghats-on-diwali-eve/articleshow/135637323.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ayodhya-glows-with-30-lakh-diyas-as-deepotsav-lights-up-saryu-ghats-on-diwali-eve/articleshow/135637323.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-07T18:26:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135637473,imgsize-199822.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Penguin was 'uneasy' with criticism of govt: Sonia Gandhi's 1st reaction to memoir row]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/penguin-was-uneasy-with-criticism-of-govt-sonia-gandhis-1st-reaction-to-memoir-row/articleshow/135636722.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135636722.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Sonia Gandhi voiced her dismay over Penguin Random House India's decision to withdraw her memoir, 'Belonging: A Journey of Love', due to disagreements about sensitive subjects involving Prime Minister Narendra Modi. She interpreted this as an effort to inhibit her narrative and suggested possible government influence.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/penguin-was-uneasy-with-criticism-of-govt-sonia-gandhis-1st-reaction-to-memoir-row/articleshow/135636722.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/penguin-was-uneasy-with-criticism-of-govt-sonia-gandhis-1st-reaction-to-memoir-row/articleshow/135636722.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-07T17:59:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135636824,imgsize-111620.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Poor Biharis don't know anything': Congress UP in-charge Rajendra Pal Gautam targets BJP chief Nitin Nabin]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/poor-biharis-dont-know-anything-congress-up-in-charge-rajendra-pal-gautam-targets-bjp-chief-nitin-nabin/articleshow/135635083.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135635083.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/poor-biharis-dont-know-anything-congress-up-in-charge-rajendra-pal-gautam-targets-bjp-chief-nitin-nabin/articleshow/135635083.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/poor-biharis-dont-know-anything-congress-up-in-charge-rajendra-pal-gautam-targets-bjp-chief-nitin-nabin/articleshow/135635083.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-07T17:55:16+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135636772,imgsize-103545.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Army debunks Pakistan propaganda about 'Chinese troops inside Arunachal']]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/army-debunks-pakistan-propaganda-about-chinese-troops-inside-arunachal/articleshow/135636159.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135636159.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Indian Army has strongly refuted false reports on social media suggesting that Chinese forces made significant territorial gains in Arunachal Pradesh. Claims of a 50 km advance in early November were thoroughly investigated, revealing six accounts deliberately pushing misleading information. Official sources assure that there has been no major defeat of Indian troops, emphasizing the importance of relying on credible sources for updates on border issues to combat misinformation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/army-debunks-pakistan-propaganda-about-chinese-troops-inside-arunachal/articleshow/135636159.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/army-debunks-pakistan-propaganda-about-chinese-troops-inside-arunachal/articleshow/135636159.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-07T17:41:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135636284,imgsize-157968.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Evening newswrap: Tech exec shot dead in Faridabad over parking spot; Iran claims its forces have downed 260 aircraft, and more]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-newswrap-tech-exec-shot-dead-in-faridabad-over-parking-spot-iran-claims-its-forces-have-downed-260-aircraft-and-more/articleshow/